# den instance oauth

den wrote this file when it created this VM. It lists the repos this VM can reach.

- Nest: `oauth`, declared in /p/dev-home/den.yaml
- Template: `digitaleo`
- Start folder: /p/dev-home

## Mounted repos

- oauth.messengeo.net — /p/oauth.messengeo.net
- libeo — /p/libeo (optional) (worktree, branch feature/x)
- public.mcp — /p/public.mcp (key js.public-mcp)

## Repos of the nest not mounted

- js.box — host path /p/js.box (optional)

## Other repos of this machine

- php.flow — host path /p/php.flow

A repo missing from "Mounted repos" is not available in this VM. Say so, and ask the human to add it: `den rm oauth`, then `den up oauth --repo <host path>`, or add the repo to the nest. Do not look for it elsewhere and do not clone it.

The same data as JSON is in the file named by the environment variable `DEN_REPOS`.
